{"bill":{"id":"119-sres-204","congress":119,"billType":"sres","billNumber":"204","title":"A resolution recognizing escalating threats to freedom of the press and freedom of speech worldwide, including increasing harm to journalists reporting in conflict zones and under repressive regimes, reaffirming the vital role that a free and independent press plays in upholding democracy, fostering economic prosperity, and keeping the public informed, and reaffirming freedom of the press as a priority of the United States Government in supporting democracy, human rights, and good governance in commemoration of \"World Press Freedom Day\" on May 3, 2025.","introducedDate":"2025-05-05","latestActionDate":"2025-05-05","latestActionText":"Referred to the Committee on Foreign Relations. (text: CR S2759-2760)","policyArea":"International Affairs","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"S001194","cosponsorBioguideIds":["T000476","K000384","M001176","V000128","C001088","D000563","S001150","B001288","W000779"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"This resolution recognizes the centrality of a free press to free societies and democratic governance and expresses concerns about threats to the exercise of freedom of expression globally.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-resolution/204","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/sres/BILLSTATUS-119sres204.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:30:59.104Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-sres-204","plainSummary":"This resolution recognizes the importance of a free press to democracy and expresses concern about threats to journalists and freedom of expression around the world. It reaffirms that supporting press freedom is a priority for U.S. foreign policy in promoting democracy and human rights. As a resolution, it does not change any law or create new obligations; it is a formal statement of the Senate's position.","industries":[{"industry":"media-enter